course: dictionary
lesson: 15705
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word topknot can name a hairstyle, and it can also name a tuft of feathers on a bird. To find out which meaning is used, read the words around it. Those words are its context.
explain: «Mia tied her hair in a topknot before the race.» Here Mia has her hair gathered into a bun on top of her head. «The crested duck had a topknot of feathers.» Now the words duck and feathers tell you the topknot is on a bird.
explain: Ask yourself: what would fit here, a bun of hair or a tuft of feathers? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A topknot is hair tied in a knot or bun on the top of the head.
fact: A topknot can also be a tuft of feathers or hair on top of the head of a bird or animal, like some ducks, chickens and dogs.
fact: «Tie a topknot» means gather your hair and tie it up on top of your head, and «a messy topknot» is a bun that looks a bit untidy.
fact: In many Sikh families, boys tie their long hair in a topknot, called a joora or patka, as part of their faith.
fact: Samurai warriors in Japan wore their hair in a topknot.
exercise: «Mia tied her hair in a topknot before the race.» What is a topknot here? | A ribbon tied around the wrist | A hat made of feathers | *A bun of hair on top of the head | A long plait down the back
exercise: What does the topknot belong to in «The crested duck had a topknot of feathers»? | *A duck | A kitchen window | A tall tree | A girl with long hair
exercise: Ravi says a topknot is only a hairstyle. Is he right? | Yes, it means a kind of hat | Yes, it only ever means hair | No, it means a type of shoe | *No, it can also be a tuft of feathers on a bird
test: «His messy topknot fell over one eye.» What does messy suggest? | Neat and tidy | Shiny and new | Wet from the rain | *Untidy, with loose strands of hair
test: Which of these is a topknot on an animal? | A spotted tail on a cat | A long beard on a goat | A stripe along a horse's back | *A tuft of feathers on top of a chicken's head
exam: Which sentence uses topknot to mean a hairstyle? | «The rain made the path slippery.» | «The ferry left the harbour at noon.» | *«Sam tied his long hair in a topknot.» | «The crested duck showed off its topknot.»
